MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The carbide burrs fit the work I could do after drilling and cutting: smoothing holes and shaping edges, provided they fit my tool.",
    "Threaded magnetic mounts and E-clips offer useful fastening options beyond my bolts, rivets and cotter pins, while duct tape complements my existing tapes for temporary repairs."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The pressure gauge and pipe tee require a particular pressure or plumbing project that my recent purchases do not establish; simply being workshop supplies does not make them useful to me now.",
    "Another M4–M6 bolt kit overlaps my recent assortment. The construction adhesive is relevant, but three tubes would need a specific project, and the long pegboard hooks require a setup I have not established."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in tools and repair supplies seems to have been stretched into a need for specialized plumbing parts and rod magnets.",
    "Buying hardware assortments seems to have been taken as a reason to suggest more assortments, even when the sizes repeat supplies I recently acquired."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I value supplies that extend what I can do with my existing equipment, such as finishing drilled holes or adding removable mounts, more than items that merely look related.",
    "Immediate usefulness depends on compatibility, existing supplies and project needs: tool shank size, mounting arrangements and package quantity can determine whether I would choose an otherwise relevant item."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my fabrication and repair interests, but sometimes confused related workshop supplies with useful additions to what I already have."
}
